          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nâkhongir is nâkhon, \"nail\", with -gir, \"taking\" (from gereftan, \"to take\"): the nail-taker. Both are native; nâkhon is usually traced to Middle Persian nāxun."
            }
          ]
        },
